---
/**
 * Hope for Healing page (/hope-for-healing/): the rescue's medical fund.
 * Sections: fund story + donate → current recipients (one .story per dog) →
 * closing donate band.
 *
 * To add or remove a recipient, copy or delete one <article class="story">.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { donateUrl } from "../data/site";
import hopeSign from "../assets/images/hope-sign.jpg";
import fiona from "../assets/images/fiona.jpg";
import zoey from "../assets/images/zoey.jpg";
import shelby from "../assets/images/shelby.jpg";
import healingCone from "../assets/images/healing-cone.jpg";
---
<Base
  title="Hope for Healing | Davis Dog Farm"
  description="Hope for Healing pays for medical care for foster dogs and helps community members afford vet care."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h1>Hope for Healing</h1>
        <p>This fund pays for medical care for our foster dogs, and helps people in our community who are struggling to afford care for their own dogs.</p>
        <p>Hope was a sweet girl fostered by Janea through Rebound Hounds. She had a cancerous facial tumor, and generous private donors paid for her treatment. Hope lost her battle with cancer on February 11, 2021. In her name, we try to give other dogs the same chance.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-donate" href={donateUrl}>Donate to Hope for Healing</a>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted note">In PayPal, add the note “Hope for Healing” so your gift goes to this fund.</p>
      </div>
      <Image src={hopeSign} alt="A hand-painted sign reading HOPE with paw prints" width={720} class="tall" loading="eager" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-white">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Dogs the fund is helping</h2>

      <article class="story">
        <Image src={fiona} alt="Princess Fiona looking out a window" width={520} />
        <div>
          <h3>Princess Fiona</h3>
          <p>Fiona was thrown away when the person who bought her found out she wasn’t “perfect.” She was passed along twice more to people who didn’t want her either, because she needed vet care, and then she was scheduled to be euthanized.</p>
          <p>There was no way we’d let that happen to such a sweet, gentle girl without giving her a chance to get better.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="story">
        <Image src={zoey} alt="Zoey resting in her foster’s lap after eye surgery" width={520} />
        <div>
          <h3>Zoey <span class="aka">(formerly Maggie)</span></h3>
          <p>Zoey came to us as a surrender with entropion, eyelids that roll inward so the lashes rub the eye. One eye was swollen almost shut. She also had large patches of missing hair and irritated skin.</p>
          <p>She’s now home with her amazing foster family after her entropion surgery. Look how beautiful her eyes are.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="story">
        <Image src={shelby} alt="Shelby, a tan puppy, held in her foster’s arms" width={520} />
        <div>
          <h3>Shelby <span class="aka">(formerly Quinn)</span></h3>
          <p>Shelby arrived with an upper respiratory infection and wouldn’t put weight on her front left leg. She’s been seen by our vet and is healing with her foster family.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-ink">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Help the next dog</h2>
        <p>Every surgery, prescription and follow-up visit on this page was paid for by people like you.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-donate" href={donateUrl}>Donate to Hope for Healing</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Image src={healingCone} alt="A dog in a recovery cone looking up at the camera" width={800} class="tall" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
